sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Image Analysis and Human Verification Sequence
  accDescr: Ordered calls and returns for upload, real inference, storage, database persistence and human feedback. Notes distinguish API revision from the current UI.
  participant B as Browser
  participant N as Next.js
  participant A as FastAPI modules
  participant D as PostgreSQL
  B->>N: Submit image<br/>/api/detectra/analyze
  N->>A: POST /analyze
  Note over A: Validate MIME, size, decode<br/>Run YOLO inference<br/>Save image file
  A->>D: Insert model/image/detections<br/>Commit analysis
  D-->>A: Persisted records
  A-->>N: 201 analysis result
  N-->>B: Validate and map result<br/>Display labels, boxes, scores
  B->>N: Submit reviewer and verdict<br/>/api/detectra/verify
  N->>A: Verify detection
  A->>D: Lock image and detection<br/>Insert review, relink detection<br/>Update image totals
  D-->>A: Review record<br/>Commit on successful request
  A-->>N: 201 saved review
  N-->>B: Validate review ID<br/>Show saved verdict
  Note over B,D: Reload restores saved feedback. Repeated API verification creates<br/>a new review and replaces its link. The UI has no revision button.
  Note over B,D: An empty-result review attaches to the image. Incorrect means<br/>a missed target. It does not create a detection or bounding box.
  Note over B,D: Invalid input is rejected. Known failed writes roll back and delete<br/>the saved file. An uncertain commit retains it. Unconfirmed reviews<br/>are not displayed as saved. Model and storage calls are grouped<br/>within FastAPI above. Figure 3 shows their separate modules.
